From 0cd40d1a9cc418a548e1f0d4133bcb59204c8eca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JoshuaHayesWasHere <josh.hayes121@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:35:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): jstack tree rows approve, remove and answer
 through the task's home, and show the brief jbus keeps

Approve, Remove from queue and Answer on a task row each send the task's own home a user
message ("approve <slug> (brief sha <sha12>)", "remove <slug>", "answer question <n> (<slug>): <text>"),
which the home acts on as the user's word; the server runs no jbus write. Open brief reads
jbus/<repo>/briefs/<slug>.md through a new read-only jbus.readBrief RPC, with the sha jbus checks
an approval against, and Approve lives in that dialog so a go names the brief the user read.
A task's open question gets an inline answer row under it. JbusTask's waitsOnUser becomes
waitsOn: approval, answer or word.
